meta {
  name: sign in, so the forgery attempt carries a real session
  type: http
  seq: 19
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-in/email
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "e2e@test.local",
    "password": "e2e-test-password-123"
  }
}

docs {
  Deliberately asserts nothing. The next two cases have to attempt key creation
  *as a signed-in user* — a request with no session would be refused for want of
  one, and would pass whether or not the endpoint is actually blocked. Where a
  bootstrapped account exists this leaves a cookie behind; where it doesn't, the
  next cases still hold, because they assert the block's own message rather than
  a bare status.
}
